60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option C is out. A whole-building let in another prefecture is a financial disaster waiting to happen with the cancellation risks.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Option B is impossible. The hall's timetable is already fragmented. We'd be training in shifts, which is a disaster for recovery and sleep.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option A seems okay, but is the reservation system the one with the lottery? If so, it's a lot of work for the organizers.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A is the only viable choice. It's a public facility with fixed rates and it's inland, which keeps transport costs low and predictable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A has shared dorms. That's exactly what we need to break the year-group barriers. It's the only one that solves the social problem.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Minato, even if the reservation is tedious, it's a one-time administrative cost. The financial risk of Option C is a recurring liability.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Takumi, as long as the dorms are actually beds and not just mats on a floor. I want to ensure the training quality doesn't suffer.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I see. If the only other options are a scheduling nightmare or a financial risk, then the administrative work of Option A is the lesser evil.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"Exactly. Option A provides a hard cost per person. No hidden fees, no transport spikes. It's the only way to ensure the club account stays healthy.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shion, it's a sports facility. They have proper beds. The point is that we'll be in the same space, not separated by distance or schedules.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"Logically, Option A is the only choice that minimizes financial uncertainty and provides a stable environment for the whole group.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"I can accept Option A. It's a professional facility, which means the environment is controlled. It's far superior to the chaos of Option B.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm worried about the paperwork, but if everyone agrees, I'll help with the application so one person doesn't have to do it all.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm glad we're agreeing. We cannot risk another budget deficit. Option A is the most fiscally responsible choice we have.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I'm voting for A. It's the only way we'll actually function as a single club instead of three separate year-groups.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Then we are in agreement. Option A is the most rational choice for the club's stability and the members' fairness.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,Agreed. Stability in the environment leads to stability in performance.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm glad we're all on the same page. I'll make sure the workload is shared.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Good. Let's commit to Option A before the booking window opens.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"Finally. Let's actually make this camp about the people, not just the practice.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
